                <pb facs="1103" n="967" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg967"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.1515/962: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-10-30T18:00:00-06:00">October 30, 1929—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 31—1:43 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>105. The Minister for Foreign Affairs stated to me today that Honduras will
                    accept the proposal contained in your telegram No. 78, October 25, 5 p.m., but
                    that the acceptance may not be forwarded until next week.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Guatemala.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
